course: dictionary
lesson: 4608
title: Hibernation: a deep winter sleep
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hibernation is a science word, and the lessons around it give you clues. «Hedgehogs wake from hibernation thin and hungry» tells you that hibernation is a long rest, and that the animal has used up its food while resting.
explain: Look for the sentence that explains the word. «Hibernation is a long, deep winter sleep in which the body temperature drops and the heart beats slowly.» Here the author tells you the meaning straight away: the body cools and the heart slows down.
explain: Context can also show you how big a word is. «Hibernation is something much bigger than a long nap» tells you that it is not just a nap. The animal lives on its stored fat through the hungry time of winter. When you meet a word like this, swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Hibernation is a very deep, sleep-like rest that some animals go into during winter.
fact: Animals such as hedgehogs, dormice, bats, some bears and ground squirrels hibernate.
fact: Before hibernating, animals eat a lot in autumn to store fat, so they have food for the hungry winter.
fact: During hibernation, the body temperature drops and the heart beats slowly.
fact: Informally, «hibernation» can mean a long time of staying inside and resting.
exercise: «Hedgehogs wake from hibernation thin and hungry.» What does hibernation mean here? | A hot summer holiday by the sea | A long walk in the rain | *A very deep, sleep-like rest through winter | A quick nap after lunch
exercise: «Animals eat a lot in autumn to store fat.» Why do they store fat? | To stay awake all winter | To make their coats thicker in spring | *To live on it through the hungry winter
exercise: «If you find a hibernating animal, do not wake it.» What should you do? | Wake it up to check it is alive | Carry it into the warm house and shake it gently | *Leave it alone and do not wake it
test: «Waking up from hibernation burns a lot of stored fat that has to last the winter.» What does the stored fat have to do? | Be thrown away in spring | *Last through the winter | Keep the animal awake all day
test: Sam says, «I've been in hibernation all weekend, just on the sofa.» What does hibernation mean here? | Running around the park | *A long time of staying inside and resting | A deep winter sleep with a cooling body | A visit to the zoo
exam: Jayden says hibernation is just a long nap. Is he right? | No, it is a summer holiday for bats | Yes, it is exactly the same as a nap | *No, the body cools, the heart slows and the animal lives on stored fat
